      "beats": [
        {
          "say": "Lexical search connects a query to terms in the indexed text. An inverted index maps a term to the records containing it. Searching for tomato activates its posting list, avoiding a fresh reading of every book in the collection.",
          "start": 0.4,
          "end": 14.728,
          "duration": 14.328,
          "until": 15.278
        },
        {
          "say": "BM25 adjusts these matches using term rarity, repeated occurrences, and document length. Repeating a word has diminishing returns. A rare catalog code can be especially useful, provided the query and document analyzer preserve that code in compatible forms.",
          "start": 15.278,
          "end": 32.486,
          "duration": 17.208,
          "until": 33.236
        },
        {
          "say": "Now ask for growing tomatoes while a passage says raising tomato plants. Stemming or learned sparse expansion may help. For this deliberately simple word matcher, the phrase changes remove useful overlap. That leaves an opening for the semantic lane.",
          "start": 33.236,
          "end": 47.66,
          "duration": 14.424,
          "until": 48.209999999999994
        }
      ],
